# Apps generated by running the examples/ prompts (disposable test output)
examples/*-app/
__pycache__/

# Local IDE/editor settings (personal, not project-shared)
.vscode/

# Filled-in copy of inspector-config.example.json — carries a real project URL and
# API key, so it must never be committed. The .example.json alongside it is what
# ships.
inspector-config.json

# Raw screen recordings behind the demo GIFs. Tens of MB each and regenerable
# from examples/demos/build-demo-gif.py, so only the GIFs are committed.
*.mov

# Playwright profile used by the demo recorder. Holds real logged-in sessions for
# the portals the demos walk through, so it must stay local.
examples/demos/.profile/
# Raw Playwright captures, converted to GIFs by build-demo-gif.py
examples/demos/recordings/

# OpenSpec generates per-agent skill and command mirrors from openspec/ — they are
# build output, not source. They are also visible to the `skills` CLI, whose
# discovery is additive across agent directories and cannot be filtered at install
# time (`-s` takes exact names, not globs), so committing them means anyone running
# `npx skills add formio/ai` is offered this repo's OpenSpec and TDD workflow
# skills alongside the Form.io library. Regenerate locally with the OpenSpec CLI.
#
# The .claude/skills/formio-* symlinks into plugin/skills/ are NOT ignored: they are
# how this repo's own sessions load the library, and the skills CLI skips them
# because it does not follow symlinks during discovery.
.claude/skills/openspec-*/
.claude/skills/tdd-*/
.cursor/skills/
.github/skills/

# Output of `npx skills add <source>` run inside this working tree — third-party
# skill libraries a maintainer installed for their own sessions (e.g.
# `angular/skills`), never this repository's source. The CLI writes the same
# library twice, once per frontmatter dialect: `.agents/skills/` for agents that
# read the shared location and `agent/skills/` for those that read the singular
# one, plus `.claude/skills/<name>` symlinks into `.agents/` and a
# `skills-lock.json` recording each source and hash. All of it is regenerable by
# re-running the installer, and committing it would offer someone else's skills to
# anyone running `npx skills add formio/ai` here — the same additive-discovery
# problem the OpenSpec mirrors above describe. `.claude/skills/formio-*` remains
# tracked, because those symlinks point into this repository's own plugin/skills/.
.agents/
agent/
.claude/skills/angular-*
skills-lock.json

# Initiative working notes — useful to whoever is doing the work, residue to
# everyone else. Both stay on a maintainer's disk and out of the public tree.
#
# MARKETPLACE.md tracks third-party review queues (Cursor marketplace, Codex
# directory, awesome-copilot, the MCP registries) whose status moves between
# releases. The release behaviour it depends on is specified instead: review-gated
# channels are never automated and a pending submission never fails a release.
#
# docs/multi-agent-portability.md is the audit and phase plan for the multi-agent
# portability work. The durable record is the OpenSpec change set — motivation in
# each proposal, decisions in each design — so a committed roadmap only duplicates
# it and ages into something that reads as current planning.
/MARKETPLACE.md
docs/multi-agent-portability.md
